# Icon buttons, not text buttons

Text-labeled buttons are the default only for a primary or ambiguous action.
Every other control ships as an icon. Do not wait to be asked.

## Icon-only is required for

Compact, secondary, repeated, toolbar, row, header, and pane actions whenever a
widely understood glyph exists:

| Action | Glyph | Action | Glyph |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| new / add | `fa-plus` | delete / remove | `fa-trash` |
| edit | `fa-pen` | view / preview | `fa-eye` |
| send | `fa-paper-plane` | refresh / sync | `fa-arrows-rotate` |
| approve | `fa-check` | close / cancel | `fa-xmark` |
| open external | `fa-arrow-up-right-from-square` | archive | `fa-box-archive` |

Place them flush right on the block's title row so the action bar reads as one
line and the content below keeps the vertical space.

## Composition (every icon control)

`fw-button fw-surface fw-surface-thin fw-icon-button` at
`--fw-icon-control-size`, plus an `aria-label` and a matching `title`, an
`aria-hidden` `fa-solid` glyph, and `fa-spinner fa-spin` while busy. A field
caption replaced by an icon moves to the input's `aria-label`.

## Keep visible text only when

The action is primary or has no clear glyph (Sign in, entity Create / Save) —
then pair the text with a leading icon. OAuth / “Sign in with …” controls keep
visible provider text **and** a leading brand glyph when one exists. Backend
action renderers populate the payload icon rather than shipping a text-only
label.

## Stable chrome

Icon-only secondaries keep peer-route headers from shifting when labels differ
in width. Prefer a fixed trailing action order per surface; do not mix a
text-labeled secondary next to icon-only neighbors on the same bar.
